  "date": "2026-08-16",
  "purpose": "At a real GPU memory-pressure point where whole-cache Q8 cannot provide safe residency but whole-cache Q5 can (SmolLM2-360M, ctx=180000, real GTX 1650), test H1: does a profile-selected mixed Q8/Q5 layout retain some Q8 layers at the same practical residency as whole-cache Q5, with measurably better quality against a true F16 ground-truth reference -- the terminal, apples-to-apples comparison Phase 11D left open.",
  "literal_verdict": "CONSTRAINED_MIXED_WORKS_BUT_NO_QUALITY_WIN",
  "verdict_summary": "Mixed KV mechanically fits at the same practical residency as whole-cache Q5 at the primary constrained point (VRAM delta 276 MiB measured, matching theoretical KV-byte delta to within 1.3 MiB), and profile-based sensitivity layer placement beats every naive equal-budget layout. But measured against a true F16 reference, the best mixed configuration (top-8 Q8 layers) is measurably WORSE quality than simply staying whole-cache Q5 -- it beat Q5 on only 1 of 5 held-out prompts (mean logit_rel_l2 0.0749 vs Q5's 0.0668) -- while using more VRAM and offering no performance advantage. The measurement was clean, deterministic/bit-identical on repeat, and internally cross-validated. A second finding disclosed as a real safety caveat, not swept aside: the tighter empirical VRAM model that predicts mixed peak usage to within 0.05% produces a confirmed FALSE-SAFE result right at the real top-8/top-9 layer boundary -- not safe to productize as-is even if the quality result had gone the other way.",
  "verdict_source": "results/canonical/summary.json: decision_gate, decision_gate_rationale, quality_result, memory_safety, next_step_recommendation (literal source fields, not synthesized)",
  "productized": false,
  "product_pr": null,
  "product_commit": null,
  "productization_note": "Not productized itself -- this phase's own next_step_recommendation is to stop mixed-KV productization for the constrained-regime case and retain the product's existing whole-cache adaptive policy (PR #20, kadireren7/membrane commit d6e6189d0417858bfcf3d51c766eaa4be5fe46e1) unchanged. This phase's value is the negative result that justified NOT building a Q8->mixed->Q5 hierarchy on top of the already-shipped Q5 (PR #19, commit d101fc80d535b09adecd90345312d50774bd821c) and adaptive (PR #20) features.",
  "reproducibility": "PARTIALLY_REPRODUCIBLE",
  "hardware": "Real GTX 1650 (Vulkan backend, nvidia-smi VRAM readings) and same host's CPU",
  "models": [
    "SmolLM2-360M-Instruct-f16"
  ],
  "llama_cpp_pin": "c0bc8591e8815c63cb01dd3f051a8b0df02501c9",
  "follow_up": "None -- this is the terminal decision point of the Phase 11B-11E chain. next_step_recommendation explicitly says to stop mixed-KV productization and retain the product's current whole-cache adaptive policy unchanged; no Phase 11F was started.",
